land-atlas/florida/monroe-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Monroe County runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 41 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair came in at 37% of normal, and January to February 2026 sits at 29% so far. Grid 6196 had its driest year in 1961 at 49% of normal.</p>"}
